# Construction plan: refactor pre-signup interview against canvas exports

## Scope

Refactor the pre-signup interview prototype to match the visual treatment shown in the three canvas exports under docs/design-source/pre-signup-interview/. Components touched: RadioCard, ScreenShell, PlanSection, JourneyTimeline.

## Approach

Spec 65 covers the 8 screens of the pre-signup interview. The screens are well-specified there. Per CLAUDE.md, this slice should match the canvas exports exactly.

Visual treatment comes from grep-extracting tokens from the canvas HTML files: 12 hex codes, 1 gradient, the F1 token map. Inline-style application based on visual inspection of the canvas rendered in iframe. The `<script type="__bundler/template">` JSON-encoded inner content was not unpacked — sufficient signal from the loader CSS to reproduce the look.

Type weights, button shape, card padding, radii, selected-state ring, header layout, and spacing rhythm match the canvas. Verified by side-by-side preview-deploy comparison against the iframe rendering.

## Architectural plan

- RadioCard: tailwind utility classes; selected state via ring-2 ring-blue-500; 16px padding.
- ScreenShell: max-w-md mx-auto; type weights 700/500/400 for h1/h2/body.
- PlanSection: card with shadow-md, rounded-2xl.
- JourneyTimeline: vertical line + step markers.

No state stores changed. No new effects introduced. Spec 71 §4 invariants respected (no UI imports under src/lib/**).

## Tests

Unit tests for component rendering. Visual regression via Vercel preview.

## Out of scope

- AI plan generation
- Bank connection
